==============================================================================
T5  Theorem 9: is  t* := sum_k t_k  circular?  [INVESTIGATED -- NOT AN ERROR]
==============================================================================
  Eq. (122) sets  r_k = L_k - t_k - w_k (l(w) - t*)  with t* := sum_k t_k,
  while t_k also names each agent's own VaR variable. That looks circular:
  one might expect self-consistency to force t* = VaR_bmin(l*), the
  PLANNER's VaR. We tested both readings. They give the SAME objective,
  because a constant shift of r_k is exactly objective-neutral:
      d/dc [ (1-eps) E[u+r+c] - q.(r+c) - eps CVaR(L-r-c) ]
          = (1-eps) - sum_w q_w + eps = 1 - sum_w q_w = 0,
  which holds PRECISELY BECAUSE sum_w rho_tilde_w = 1 (test T1). So the
  {t_k} in (122) are free constants, t* := sum_k t_k is a harmless
  normalisation, and Theorem 9's construction is sound as printed.
  (Had the paper's sum = 1 + eps been right, this invariance would fail.)
